s\\{F3017226-FE2A-4295-8BDF-00C3A9A7E4C5}\nL121: \nL122:     HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Microsoft\\EdgeUpdate\\Clients\\{F3017226-FE2A-4295-8BDF-00C3A9A7E4C5}\nL123:     `\nL124:   * Approach 2: Run 【36†GetAvailableCoreWebView2BrowserVersionString】 and evaluate whether the `versionInfo` is `nullptr`. `nullptr` indicates that the WebView2 Runtime isn't installed. This API returns version information for the WebView2 Runtime or for any installed preview channels of Microsoft Edge (Beta, Dev, or Canary).\nL125: ###### Online-only deployment\nL126: \nL127: If you have an online-only deployment scenario where users are assumed to have internet access, use the following workflow.\nL128: \nL129:   1. During your app setup, run a test to make sure that the WebView2 Runtime is already installed. See 【12†Detect if a WebView2 Runtime is already installed】, above.\nL130:   2. If the Runtime isn't installed, in your app setup process, use the link (from the Get the Link button on the download page) to programmatically download the WebView2 Runtime Bootstrapper.\nL131: \nL132:   3. Invoke the WebView2 Runtime Bootstrapper by issuing the following command.\nL133: If you run the following command from an elevated process or command prompt, it triggers a per-machine install. If you don't run the command from an elevated process or command prompt, a per-user install will take place. However, a per-user install is automatically replaced by a per-machine install, if a per-machine Microsoft Edge Updater is in place. A per-machine Microsoft Edge Updater is provided as part of Microsoft Edge, except for the Canary preview channel of Microsoft Edge.\nL134: For more information, see 【11†Installing the Runtime as per-machine or per-user】.\nL135: \nL136:     `MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe /silent /install\nL137:     `\nL138: The above workflow has several benefits:\nL139: \nL140:   * The Runtime is installed only when needed.\nL141: \nL142:   * You aren't required to package a Runtime installer with your WebView2 app.\nL143: \nL144:   * The WebView2 Runtime Bootstrapper automatically detects the device's architecture (platform) and then installs the matching WebView2 Runtime.\nL145: \nL146:   * The Runtime is installed silently.\nL147: Alternatively, instead of programmatically downloading the bootstrapper on-demand by getting a link, as shown above, you can package the Evergreen Bootstrapper for the WebView2 Runtime with your app.\nL148: ###### Offline deployment\nL149: \nL150: If you have an offline deployment scenario, where app deployment has to work entirely offline, use the following workflow.\nL151: \nL152:   1. Download the Evergreen Standalone Installer from 【32†Download the WebView2 Runtime†developer.microsoft.com】 to your development machine. The Evergreen Standalone Installer installs the Evergreen WebView2 Runtime on the client.\nL153: \nL154:   2. Include the Evergreen Standalone Installer in your app installer or updater.\nL155:   3. During your app setup, run a test to make sure that the WebView2 Runtime is already installed. See 【12†Detect if a WebView2 Runtime is already installed】, above.\nL156: \nL157:   4. If the WebView2 Runtime isn't installed, run the Evergreen Standalone Installer. If you want to run a silent installation, you can run the following command.\nL158: If you run the following command from an elevated process or command prompt, it triggers a per-machine install. If you don't run the command from an elevated process or command prompt, a per-user install will take place. However, a per-user install is automatically replaced by a per-machine install, if a per-machine Microsoft Edge Updater is in place. A per-machine Microsoft Edge Updater is provided as part of Microsoft Edge, except for the Canary preview channel of Microsoft Edge.\nL159: For more information, see 【11†Installing the Runtime as per-machine or per-user】.\nL160: \nL161:     `MicrosoftEdgeWebView2RuntimeInstaller{X64/X86/ARM64}.exe /silent /install\nL162:     `\nL163: #### Handle Evergreen WebView2 Runtime updates\nL164: New versions of the Evergreen WebView2 Runtime are automatically downloaded to the client. The client uses the new version of the WebView2 Runtime when your WebView2 app is restarted. However, if your app runs continuously, your app will continue to use the previous version of the WebView2 Runtime. This has security implications, because the previous version of the WebView2 Runtime might have security vulnerabilities that are fixed in the new version.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1be15-2930-7892-b505-55fcd54bdf1e","create_time":1794190594.9772265}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
